cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AEROLAB RESILIENCE: Navigation Integrity and Resilience Validation Platform"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it. Note that it is a
  simulation-only research demonstrator and makes no claim of conformance to any
  aviation standard.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bennmane
    given-names: Benn
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bennmane27/aerolab-resilience"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-21"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic simulation test bench for evaluating the integrity and
  resilience of multi-sensor aircraft navigation architectures. It generates a
  closed-form trajectory, models GNSS, inertial, barometric and runway-relative
  vision sensors with explicit noise, bias and latency, injects thirteen families
  of synthetic fault into the measurements only, and compares five navigation
  architectures on the identical measurement stream. Its principal result is a
  measured detectability floor: the drift rate below which each integrity policy
  stops noticing that a source is lying.
keywords:
  - navigation integrity
  - sensor fusion
  - error-state Kalman filter
  - fault detection and exclusion
  - solution separation
  - GNSS resilience
  - Monte Carlo benchmarking
  - simulation
